/dim]prefix, bob-cli, is corrected by a one-off manual rename instead of[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]by shipping a general migration feature.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]revert_bead_reprefix_epic.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ez[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ez/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Revert the sase-repo bead re-prefix surface[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sase-revert[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-revert: revert the three sase-ei commits in the sase repo, keep the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unrelated forward mint guard, resolve the three known conflict files, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and prove the reverted tree still builds, lints, and passes the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead/agents_sync suites.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove the Rust alias and re-prefix primitives[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]core-revert[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-revert[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-revert: delete the sase-core bead re-prefix module, alias config [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]field, and PyO3 migration bindings, restore pre-epic bead ID resolution [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]semantics without regressing the retained single-pass detail read, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cut a patch release.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Retire the sase-ei plans, beads, and store residue[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]epic-retire[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-revert[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic-retire: remove the epic and phase plan files from the local and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sidecar plan stores, drop the id_aliases residue from the sase bead [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]store config, and close sase-ei and its unfinished phases as canceled [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with an auditable reason.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hand-fix the bob-cli bead and agent identities[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]bob-cli-reprefix[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sase-revert[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli-reprefix: rename the thirteen leaked-prefix bob-cli beads and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]their derived agent identities to a collision-free bob-cli prefix with a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one-off throwaway script, rewriting the bead store, plan refs, agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifacts, registries, chats, and the agents sidecar while leaving [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]published commit history untouched.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Audit that the epic left nothing behind[/bold #D7AFFF]                       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]final-audit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-revert, epic-retire, bob-cli-reprefix[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]final-audit: run the full sase and sase-core verification gates, confirm[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]no re-prefix code surface or leaked-prefix bead token survives outside [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]immutable git history, and record the outcome on the tracking bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ez","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-ez.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-195bc916bacf2ca2f7255767efa92125","started_at":"2026-08-03T18:45:58.573695+00:00","state":"active"},{"c